  "claim": "A hockey team calls the venue of the Survivor Series (2011) PPV event it's home. That team, along with the New York Islanders, and National Basketball Association NHL franchise, are popular in the New York metropolitan area.",
  "evidencia": "Page: 1974–75 New York Islanders season. Sentence: In the first round of the playoffs, New York defeated the New York Rangers in three games to advance to the Quarter-finals, where the team defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games, after they had lost the first three.\nPage: New York Rangers. Sentence: The Rangers are one of three NHL franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and New York Islanders.\nPage: Madison Square Garden. Sentence: It is home to the New York Rangers of the National Hockey League (NHL), the New York Knicks of the National Basketball Association (NBA), and since 1997, the New York Liberty (WNBA).\nPage: Survivor Series (2011). Sentence: Survivor Series (2011) was a professional wrestling pay-per-view (PPV) event produced by WWE that took place on November 20, 2011 at Madison Square Garden in New York City.",
