        "original_id": "738b9ae6-5acb-58aa-9ef3-e08beea6e690",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: New York Islanders, New York Rangers, Pittsburgh Penguins, New Jersey Devils, New York Knicks, New York Liberty, WWE, NHL, NBA, WNBA\n- Places: Madison Square Garden, New York City, New York metropolitan area\n- Events: 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, Survivor Series (2011)\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the New York Rangers in three games in the first round.\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders then defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games in the quarter-finals after losing the first three games.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three NHL franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and New York Islanders.\n- Since 1997, Madison Square Garden has been home to the New York Liberty of the WNBA.\n- Madison Square Garden is home to the New York Rangers of the NHL and the New York Knicks of the NBA.\n- On November 20, 2011, WWE produced Survivor Series (2011) at Madison Square Garden in New York City.",
